class.description:
Runs local inference through a selected provider. Add this node to the scene tree, connect its signals, set [member GodotChorus.model_path] and call [method GodotChorus.load_model]. Wait for [signal GodotChorus.model_loaded] before submitting requests. The Echo provider can be used without a model file for integration testing.
Methods must be called from the node's host thread. Background work is delivered as signals during node processing, so keep the node in the tree with processing enabled while awaiting results. Each accepted request receives exactly one terminal success or error signal; immediate rejection emits no request signals. Provider validation and prompt-fitting errors may arrive after admission.
Request admission freezes input values, history and generation defaults. Later edits do not change accepted work. All nodes share generation choices imported from the selected project JSON; configure these under [code]chorus/generation[/code] in Project Settings. Request choices take precedence. See [ChorusProjectSettings] for persistence.
Provider load options appear dynamically in the Inspector for the selected provider. Changes to provider, model path, load options or logging affect the next accepted load, not the running engine. Replacing an engine releases the old engine before loading its successor. Explicit stop and node destruction block until cleanup finishes; cancellation admission does not wait for cleanup.
[codeblock]
func _ready():
    $GodotChorus.model_loaded.connect(_on_model_loaded)
    $GodotChorus.model_load_failed.connect(_on_model_load_failed)
    $GodotChorus.generation_complete.connect(_on_generation_complete)
    $GodotChorus.generation_error.connect(_on_generation_error)
    $GodotChorus.model_path = "res://models/model.gguf"
    var load_result = $GodotChorus.load_model()
    if not load_result.accepted:
        push_error(load_result.message)

func _on_model_loaded(_load_id, _model_id):
    var request = ChorusRequest.chat(&"guide", "Where should I go?")
    request.max_tokens = 128
    var result = $GodotChorus.generate(request)
    if not result.accepted:
        push_error(result.message)

func _on_model_load_failed(_load_id, _model_id, _error, message):
    push_error(message)

func _on_generation_complete(_request_id, _session, _message_id, content, _reasoning):
    print(content)

func _on_generation_error(_request_id, _session, _error, message):
    push_error(message)
[/codeblock]
